{"search_index": 1, "query": "Gemini 3 Pro release date November 2025 Google announcement", "backend": "agentcore", "num_results": 1, "results": [{"index": 0, "title": "Introducing Gemini 3 Pro for Gemini app", "url": "https://workspaceupdates.googleblog.com/2025/11/introducing-gemini-3-pro-for-gemini-app.html", "snippet": "November 18, 2025 Introducing Gemini 3 Pro for Gemini app Gemini App Rapid Release Scheduled Release What’s changing We’re bringing our most intelligent model, Gemini 3, to the Gemini app for Google Workspace customers. This update brings state-of-the-art reasoning to your most complex problems, setting a new bar for AI model performance and delivering a more powerful and helpful experience. 

Starting today, you can try our first model of the series, Gemini 3 Pro, by selecting “Thinking” from the model drop down menu in the Gemini app on desktop, mobile app, and mobile web. Gemini 3 is starting to roll out globally to users over the age of 18 in all countries and languages where the Gemini app is available. 

Getting started Admins: The Gemini app and related in-app tools are controlled by the Generative AI settings in the Workspace Admin console. The Gemini 3 Pro model is subject to these existing controls. Visit the Help Center for more information on turning the Gemini app on or off . End users: End users who have access to the Gemini app will receive the new 3 Pro model update automatically. "}], "web_search_calls": 2, "web_searches_remaining": 1, "belief": {"p": 0.5, "base_rate_anchor": "", "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "key_uncertainties": [], "confidence": "low", "searches_tried": ["Google Gemini Pro model release 2025 2026", "Gemini 3 Pro release date November 2025 Google announcement"], "step": 0}, "hint": "Call lookup_url on a promising result URL to read the full page."}

{"search_index": 1, "query": "silver SI futures volatility May 2026 supply demand market outlook", "backend": "agentcore", "num_results": 1, "results": [{"index": 0, "title": "Silver Momentum Signals Buy-the-Dip Setup Ahead of May 15 Window", "url": "https://uk.investing.com/analysis/silver-momentum-signals-buythedip-setup-ahead-of-may-15-window-200624549", "snippet": "Silver Momentum Signals Buy-the-Dip Setup Ahead of May 15 Window Published 12/05/2026, 07:34 Silver futures continue to demonstrate powerful bullish momentum as the market accelerates toward the Weekly Sell 2 resistance zone at $88.79. The current rally reflects what the VC PMI methodology identifies as a hyperbolic phase, where momentum expands beyond equilibrium and confirms that traders should “buy corrections only” rather than aggressively fading strength. 

The market has now decisively exceeded the Daily VC PMI Mean Price at $84.15 and pushed through the weekly Sell 1 target near $84.83, activating the higher Daily Sell 2 objective at $88.78. Price action reaching an intraday high near $87.79 confirms expanding volatility and suggests the probability remains elevated for a continuation move toward the upper extreme resistance band between $88.79 and $89.76. 

The Square of 9 geometry aligns with this acceleration phase, projecting a critical cycle resistance window into May 13–15. This timing cluster suggests increased volatility and the potential for a temporary exhaustion spike before another consolidation phase develops. Should silver sustain close above the Weekly Sell 2 level at $88.79, the next Square of 9 harmonic projection targets the psychological $90–$92 range. "}], "web_search_calls": 2, "web_searches_remaining": 1, "belief": {"p": 0.5, "base_rate_anchor": "", "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "key_uncertainties": [], "confidence": "low", "searches_tried": ["silver price forecast May June 2026 CME futures market analysis", "silver SI futures volatility May 2026 supply demand market outlook"], "step": 0}, "hint": "Call lookup_url on a promising result URL to read the full page."}

{"search_index": 1, "query": "Discord IPO expected valuation price range billions 2026", "backend": "agentcore", "num_results": 2, "results": [{"index": 0, "title": "Discord’s Confidential IPO: Can “Community as Capital” Justify a $7B+ Valuation?", "url": "https://medium.com/analysts-corner/discords-confidential-ipo-can-community-as-capital-justify-a-7b-valuation-f8ad8d20cee8", "snippet": "The Buy Code 10 min readApr 6, 2026 Press enter or click to view image in full size Discord’s confidential IPO filing in January 2026 is more than a capital-raising event; it’s a stress test of whether a community-first platform can sustain a multibillion‑dollar valuation in a tougher tech market. With secondary markets implying a $7–8 billion valuation — well below its prior $14–15 billion private mark — Discord’s debut will hinge on investors finally pricing community as a form of capital, not just a soft metric in a pitch deck. 

- From $15B Darling To $7–8B Reality Check Press enter or click to view image in full size Discord’s IPO narrative begins with a comedown. In 2021 the company raised $500 million at a roughly $14.7–15.2 billion valuation, cementing its status as one of the most highly valued private communication platforms of its era. Since then, a combination of higher interest rates, tighter IPO windows, and skepticism toward unprofitable growth has pushed secondary market estimates for Discord’s equity down to the $7–10 billion range. 

Bloomberg’s reporting on the January 2026 confidential filing highlights implied valuations of $7–8 billion in secondary trading venues like Caplight and Forge, signaling that late‑stage investors are discounting the 2021 peak. Other analyses still point to an internal ambition closer to $10–15 billion, but prediction markets and private‑market prices suggest the final IPO pricing could land meaningfully lower. This creates a fascinating tension: Discord’s user and revenue metrics have grown substantially, yet its headline val"}, {"index": 1, "title": "Can it fetch $25B valuation after rejecting Microsoft? — TFN", "url": "https://techfundingnews.com/discord-ipo-q1-25bn-valuation-microsoft-rejection/", "snippet": "Working with Goldman Sachs and JPMorgan, the chat platform now boasts over 200 million monthly active users and aims to capitalise on an IPO market, fuelled by stable rates and AI momentum.​ Discord, founded in 2015 by Jason Citron and Stan Vishnevskiy, last raised $500 million at a $15 billion valuation in 2021, having evolved from gamer chats into broader communities, with Nitro subscriptions driving revenue. Leadership shifted in 2025 with Humam Sakhnini as CEO.​ "}], "web_search_calls": 2, "web_searches_remaining": 1, "belief": {"p": 0.5, "base_rate_anchor": "", "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "key_uncertainties": [], "confidence": "low", "searches_tried": ["Discord IPO 2026 valuation market cap filing", "Discord IPO expected valuation price range billions 2026"], "step": 0}, "hint": "Call lookup_url on a promising result URL to read the full page."}

{"search_index": 0, "query": "Humanity's Last Exam AI benchmark leaderboard Claude Anthropic scores 2024 2025", "backend": "agentcore", "num_results": 1, "results": [{"index": 0, "title": "Humanity's Last Exam: The AI Benchmark for LLM Reasoning", "url": "https://intuitionlabs.ai/articles/humanitys-last-exam-ai-benchmark", "snippet": "Humanity's Last Exam: The AI Benchmark for LLM Reasoning October 25, 2025 Updated March 4, 2026 30 min read Learn about Humanity's Last Exam (HLE), the Nature-published AI benchmark testing true LLM reasoning with 2,500 expert-level questions. Updated with 2026 leaderboard scores from GPT-5, Claude Opus, and Gemini 3. 

Humanity’s Last Exam (HLE) emerged as this next-level challenge. Officially launched in September 2024 by CAIS and Scale AI ([10]), HLE is designed to be “the final closed-ended academic benchmark” for AI ([2]) ([7]). The idea dates to conversations among AI safety leaders: for example, CAIS director Dan Hendrycks was reportedly spurred by Elon Musk’s remark that existing tests had become “too easy” for advanced AI ([11]). In concrete terms, HLE asks hundreds of globally recruited experts (professors, PhD students, industry specialists) to write the most difficult questions they know in their field. These questions are vetted to ensure they have unambiguous answers (suitable for automatic grading) and that the answers cannot be easily found on the internet. By focusing on highly specialized, graduate-level problems, HLE aims to measure reasoning rather than rote fact regurgitation. 

Conclusion Humanity’s Last Exam represents a milestone in AI benchmarking – one significant enough to earn publication in Nature in January 2026 ([1]). It is by design the most challenging closed-ended test assembled for machine intelligence to date, requiring genuine graduate-level reasoning across hundreds of subjects. The current outcomes – expert humans near 90% vs. the best"}], "web_search_calls": 1, "web_searches_remaining": 2, "belief": {"p": 0.5, "base_rate_anchor": "", "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "key_uncertainties": [], "confidence": "low", "searches_tried": ["Humanity's Last Exam AI benchmark leaderboard Claude Anthropic scores 2024 2025"], "step": 0}, "hint": "Call lookup_url on a promising result URL to read the full page."}

{"search_index": 2, "query": "UK government IRGC designation February 2026 Home Secretary", "backend": "agentcore", "num_results": 1, "results": [{"index": 0, "title": "U.S. and U.K. Target IRGC-QF Support to Hamas and Other Proxy Groups", "url": "https://home.treasury.gov/news/press-releases/jy1987", "snippet": "Office of Capital Access Small and Disadvantaged Business Utilization Small Business Lending Fund State Small Business Credit Initiative Daily Treasury Par Real Yield Curve Rates WASHINGTON — Today, the U.S. Department of the Treasury’s Office of Foreign Assets Control (OFAC) and the United Kingdom are jointly taking action against Iran’s Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps – Qods Force (IRGC-QF), Hamas, and Palestinian Islamic Jihad (PIJ). The U.K. is taking its first action pursuant to new Iran-related authorities, targeting eight actors, including the head of the IRGC-QF, and individuals linked to Iran’s support for Hamas and PIJ. The U.K.’s new sanctions authority has been developed to respond to unprecedented threats from the Iranian regime, including efforts to undermine peace and security across the Middle East and plots to kill individuals on U.K. soil. OFAC is designating an IRGC-QF official involved in support to Hamas. 

OFAC’s action today is being taken pursuant to Executive Order (E.O.) 13224, as amended, which targets terrorist groups and their supporters. The IRGC-QF was designated pursuant to E.O. 13224 on October 25, 2007 for providing support to multiple terrorist groups. 

Today, the U.K. is sanctioning eight actors affiliated with the IRGC-QF, Hamas, or PIJ, seven of whom have previously been designated by OFAC, including IRGC-QF commander Esmail Qaani and senior IRGC-QF official Muhammad Sa’id Izadi. IRGC-QF support has enabled Hamas’ and PIJ’s terrorist activities, to include the transfer of hundreds of millions of dollars in financial assistance and pr"}], "web_search_calls": 3, "web_searches_remaining": 0, "belief": {"p": 0.5, "base_rate_anchor": "", "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "key_uncertainties": [], "confidence": "low", "searches_tried": ["UK designate IRGC terrorist organization 2025 2026", "UK IRGC proscription Home Office terror designation", "UK government IRGC designation February 2026 Home Secretary"], "step": 0}, "hint": "Call lookup_url on a promising result URL to read the full page."}

{"search_index": 0, "query": "North Korea missile tests 2026 frequency June", "backend": "agentcore", "num_results": 1, "results": [{"index": 0, "title": "Fact Sheet: North Korea Missile Launch Activity", "url": "https://armscontrolcenter.org/fact-sheet-north-korea-missile-test-activity/", "snippet": "Kim Jong Un (2011-Present) Upon assuming leadership, Kim Jong Un undertook a concerted effort to expand and develop North Korea’s ballistic missile program. Between 2012 and 2025, North Korea has conducted more than 272 missile launches and debuted a variety of missiles with increasing ranges. Missile launch and development infrastructure has also expanded, and in some cases been established in proximity to and in connection with the state’s nuclear facilities. In 2015, the North debuted its first SLBM, the KN-11, and its first IRBM, the BM-25 Musudan, one year later, testing each several times. Multiple nuclear tests have also been conducted over this time, with the largest and most recent occurring in September 2017. 

North Korea began 2024 with a January launch of an intermediate-range ballistic missile fitted with a hypersonic glide vehicle and debuted several new systems, including the Pulhwasal-3-31 cruise missile and the Padasuri-6 anti-ship missile. Throughout the year, launches highlighted theater-range cruise and ballistic missile capabilities, culminating in October’s launch of the solid-fuel Hwasong-19 ICBM. By year’s end, North Korea had conducted at least 30 missile launches. 

North Korea conducted its first missile launch of 2025 on January 6 when it launched an upgraded version of its Hwasong-16, an intermediate-range ballistic missile fitted with a wedge-shaped payload billed as a “hypersonic glide vehicle.” According to Japanese and South Korean military intelligence, the missile flew approximately 700 miles before landing in the Sea of Japan, and althou"}], "web_search_calls": 1, "web_searches_remaining": 2, "belief": {"p": 0.5, "base_rate_anchor": "", "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "key_uncertainties": [], "confidence": "low", "searches_tried": ["North Korea missile tests 2026 frequency June"], "step": 0}, "hint": "Call lookup_url on a promising result URL to read the full page."}

{"search_index": 2, "query": "B200 GPU rental price index May June 2026", "backend": "agentcore", "num_results": 1, "results": [{"index": 0, "title": "NVIDIA B200 Cloud Pricing 2026: Per-Hour Rental Cost Across Providers vs Spheron", "url": "https://www.spheron.network/blog/nvidia-b200-cloud-pricing-2026/", "snippet": "B200 SXM6 on-demand rates range from $3.70/hr on neo-clouds to $14.24/hr on AWS in June 2026. The 3.8x price spread across providers reflects structural differences in provider margin, quota friction, and billing model, not hardware differences. The GPU is the same NVIDIA B200 SXM6 regardless of which cloud you pick. For a broader view of the B200 SXM6 specs and architecture, that guide covers memory bandwidth, FP4 throughput, and workload selection criteria in detail. At the lower end of AWS's GPU catalog, the G7 instance pricing guide covers the RTX PRO 4500 Blackwell tier, which starts at $2.52/hr and targets inference workloads under 32GB VRAM. 

What a B200 Costs to Rent in 2026 The $3.70 to $14.24/hr on-demand spread comes down to four factors. Provider tier. Neo-cloud providers (Spheron, Runpod, Lambda, Nebius) operate with lower overhead and often aggregate third-party data center supply. Hyperscalers (AWS, Azure, GCP) carry substantially higher margins and infrastructure costs. The same B200 SXM6 hardware sits at $3.70/hr on Spheron and $14.24/hr on AWS. For a full GPU cloud pricing comparison across providers and GPU models, that post covers the systematic hyperscaler premium in detail. 

Frequently Asked Questions As of June 2026, B200 SXM6 on-demand pricing ranges from $3.70/hr (Spheron) to $14.24/hr (AWS p6-b200). Lambda Labs lists B200 at $4.99-$5.29/hr, Runpod Secure Cloud at $5.89/hr, and Nebius at $5.50/hr. Spot pricing is available on Spheron from $2.74/hr/GPU and on AWS p6 spot at approximately $2.70/hr. Prices vary by provider tier, instance configuratio"}], "web_search_calls": 3, "web_searches_remaining": 0, "belief": {"p": 0.5, "base_rate_anchor": "", "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "key_uncertainties": [], "confidence": "low", "searches_tried": ["Ornn B200 Index price 2026", "Ornn B200 Index ornnai June 2026", "B200 GPU rental price index May June 2026"], "step": 0}, "hint": "Call lookup_url on a promising result URL to read the full page."}

